    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 25th slate leaning heavily on **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero** to anchor the offensive production. **Christian Yelich** is our strongest play today with a 75.84 score; he draws a highly favorable matchup against Feltner, where his 13% platoon edge and top-of-the-order usage provide a significant floor for R and RBI production. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (69.49) remains a locked-in starter, as his elite .376 xwOBA allows him to navigate a challenging matchup against Bibee, with an 11% boost derived from the SP skill profile. While **Colt Keith** (68.51) also grades out as a top-tier start, his elevated score is buoyed primarily by a premium batting order position and a favorable platoon matchup against Wacha.\n\nIn terms of bench management, the exclusion of **Josh Smith** (45.38) and **Caleb Durbin** (44.94) highlights the ruthlessness of our current efficiency requirements. **Josh Smith** came the closest to cracking the lineup, as his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Woo was compelling; however, the optimizer favored **Chase Meidroth** due to the specific weightings of today\u2019s projected game script, ultimately relegating **Josh Smith** to the bench to preserve our game caps. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.30); while his speed is a critical asset for our scarcity needs in SB, he faces the formidable Skenes, and the risk of a low-scoring performance against an elite arm is non-negligible.\n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority tonight. While **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is active, his value is uniquely tied to the 5% wind boost; any shift in atmospheric conditions could jeopardize that projection. Additionally, the presence of **Carson Benge** (46.38) in the lineup represents our lowest efficiency start, as he faces the stiff challenge of Yamamoto. We are choosing to run him out there to maintain volume, but should the game flow tilt against him, he remains the most likely candidate for an early pinch-hit replacement to keep our daily efficiency metrics aligned with the 90+ target for our core hitters.",
